2. Check vmlinux =====================================================
	readelf --debug-dump=info ./media_home1/rootfs/boot/vmlinux | grep DW_AT_comp_dir :=> check the source derectory
	readelf --debug-dump=info ./media_home1/rootfs/boot/vmlinux | grep -E 'DW_AT_comp_dir|DW_AT_name' :=> check the source derectory + name
	
	objdump --section-headers ./media_home1/rootfs/boot/vmlinux | grep debug_info 
	objdump --section-headers ./media_home1/rootfs/boot/vmlinux | grep debug_line 
		:=> check sections like .debug_info and .debug_line are present.
		
3. Check output config =====================================================
	grep -i -E "CONFIG_GPIO_OMAP=|CONFIG_KGDB=|CONFIG_KGDB_SERIAL_CONSOLE=|CONFIG_MAGIC_SYSRQ=|CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO=|CONFIG_GDB_SCRIPTS=|CONFIG_FRAME_POINTER=|CONFIG_MEDIA_TUNER_XC2028=|CONFIG_MEDIA_TUNER_XC4000" .config	
		:=>
		CONFIG_GPIO_OMAP=y
		CONFIG_MEDIA_TUNER_XC2028=m
		CONFIG_MEDIA_TUNER_XC4000=m
		CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO=y
		CONFIG_GDB_SCRIPTS=y
		CONFIG_FRAME_POINTER=y
		CONFIG_MAGIC_SYSRQ=y
		CONFIG_KGDB=y
		CONFIG_KGDB_SERIAL_CONSOLE=y
		
4. Build modules for debugging - flag =====================================================
	obj-m += gpio.o
	KDIR := /home/vinh/build_BBB_custom/linux-stable-rcn-ee
	PWD := $(shell pwd)
	CROSS_COMPILE := /home/vinh/build_BBB_custom/gcc-11.3.0-nolibc/arm-linux-gnueabi/bin/arm-linux-gnueabi-

	# Add debug flags
	ccflags-y += -O0 -g

	all:
		$(MAKE) ARCH=arm CROSS_COMPILE=$(CROSS_COMPILE) -C $(KDIR) M=$(PWD) modules

	clean:
		$(MAKE) -C $(KDIR) M=$(PWD) clean

		
5. Refer =====================================================
First, you need to have an appropriate kernel configuration. I typically set:

CONFIG_MAGIC_SYSRQ=y
CONFIG_MAGIC_SYSRQ_DEFAULT_ENABLE=0x1
CONFIG_MAGIC_SYSRQ_SERIAL=y
CONFIG_MAGIC_SYSRQ_SERIAL_SEQUENCE="g"

Setting CONFIG_MAGIC_SYSRQ_DEFAULT_ENABLE=0x1 enables all sysrq codes; setting CONFIG_MAGIC_SYSRQ_SERIAL_SEQUENCE="g" means that in order to break to the debugger we need to send <break>g.

